= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [In October 1947, who was the Maharaja of the princely state of Jammu and Kashmir who signed the Instrument of Accession with India?], (
  [Maharaja Gulab Singh], [Maharaja Hari Singh], [Sheikh Abdullah], [Karan Singh],
))

#mcq(2, [In which year did the historic Anandpur Sahib Resolution, demanding greater state autonomy, get passed by the Shiromani Akali Dal?], (
  [1966], [1971], [1973], [1984],
))

#mcq(3, [Operation Blue Star, the military assault on the Golden Temple complex in Amritsar, was conducted in which month and year?], (
  [June 1984], [October 1984], [July 1985], [January 1986],
))

#mcq(4, [The Punjab Accord of July 1985 was signed between Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi and which prominent Akali Dal leader?], (
  [Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale], [Parkash Singh Badal], [Harchand Singh Longowal], [Gurcharan Singh Tohra],
))

#mcq(5, [The Mizo National Front (MNF), which waged a 20-year armed insurgency in the Mizo Hills, was founded and led by:], (
  [Angami Zapu Phizo], [Laldenga], [Prafulla Kumar Mahanta], [Bhrigu Kumar Phukan],
))

#mcq(6, [Under the historic Assam Accord signed in August 1985, what was the mutually agreed cutoff date for the identification and deportation of illegal foreigners?], (
  [15 August 1947], [26 January 1950], [24 March 1971], [1 January 1980],
))

#mcq(7, [Which regional political party was formed in 1985 by student leaders who led the six-year-long anti-foreigner agitation in Assam?], (
  [All Assam Students Union], [Asom Gana Parishad], [Bodo People's Front], [United Minorities Front],
))

#mcq(8, [The Telugu Desam Party (TDP) was founded in 1982 on the platform of Telugu self-respect (Atma Gauravam) by which popular film icon?], (
  [M.G. Ramachandran], [N.T. Rama Rao], [Chiranjeevi], [K. Karunanidhi],
))

#mcq(9, [Which state was carved out from composite Assam in 1963 to satisfy the long-standing autonomy demand of the local tribes?], (
  [Meghalaya], [Nagaland], [Mizoram], [Manipur],
))

#mcq(10, [Following the anti-Sikh violence of 1984, which judicial inquiry commission was appointed in 2000 to submit a comprehensive report on the Delhi massacres?], (
  [Sarkaria Commission], [Shah Commission], [Nanavati Commission], [Verma Commission],
))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [Maharaja Hari Singh was the Hindu ruler of J&K who signed the Instrument of Accession on 26 October 1947 to seek Indian military aid against Pakistani tribal invaders.], answer: [B])

#solution(2, [The Anandpur Sahib Resolution was passed by the Akali Dal in 1973, articulating demands for federal restructuring, river water redistribution, and greater provincial autonomy.], answer: [C])

#solution(3, [Operation Blue Star was conducted by the Indian Army in June 1984 to eliminate armed militants led by Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale from the Golden Temple complex.], answer: [A])

#solution(4, [Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi signed the historic Memorandum of Settlement (Punjab Accord) in July 1985 with Sant Harchand Singh Longowal, President of the Akali Dal.], answer: [C])

#solution(5, [Laldenga founded the Mizo National Front (MNF) following the 1959 Mautam famine and led the armed rebellion before signing the 1986 Mizo Peace Accord to become Chief Minister.], answer: [B])

#solution(6, [The Assam Accord fixed midnight of 24 March 1971 (the eve of the Bangladesh Liberation War) as the strict cutoff date for identifying and deporting illegal immigrants.], answer: [C])

#solution(7, [AASU leaders transformed their student movement into a formal regional political party named Asom Gana Parishad (AGP) in 1985, winning the assembly elections.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [N.T. Rama Rao (NTR), legendary Telugu cinema superstar, formed the Telugu Desam Party in 1982, routing the ruling Congress in Andhra Pradesh within nine months.], answer: [B])

#solution(9, [Nagaland was granted full statehood in 1963, becoming the first tribal state carved out from composite Assam to accommodate the Naga movement.], answer: [B])

#solution(10, [The Justice G.T. Nanavati Commission of Inquiry was appointed in 2000 by the NDA government to probe the 1984 anti-Sikh riots, indicting several influential figures.], answer: [C])

